Load the cluster and its cub context into your shell:
  source [redacted].env

Deploy an app to this cluster:
  1. cub variant create <name> <base-space> --target scout-attach/target [--namespace <ns>]
  2. cub release publish <name>
Step 1 clones <base-space> into a deployment space bound to the cluster's
target and adds its Sveltos ClusterProfile to the apps space "scout-attach-sveltos-apps"; step 2
makes the deployment's config go live and, the first time, republishes the
apps space so the root profile applies the ClusterProfile. See
"cub variant create --help".
